Provisional genetic PCA reconstruction for Figure S2. Original numerical PCA scores were unavailable; these coordinates were newly calculated solely to reconstruct the required figure from the verified full38,124-SNP panel. All217 individuals were retained. Missing dosages were replaced by the observed mean dosage at each locus; loci were centered at2p and scaled by sqrt(2p(1-p)), excluding only loci with zero or invalid scaling. Explained variance refers to this reconstructed PCA, not the missing historical PCA.
Both panels display identical coordinates. The left panel uses published population classes (104individuals from9core populations and113from10peripheral populations). The right uses recovered historical individual-group assignments (101core,69peripheral,23adaptive_1,24adaptive_2) from the original easySFS popmaps. These are grouping records, not clusters inferred by this reconstruction; some AC individuals were assigned to adaptive groups despite AC's core population class. Population classes and individual genetic groups must therefore remain distinct.
No clustering, GEA discovery, demographic fitting, or optional parameter sensitivity was performed. Final-size visual checks and manuscript/supplement integration remain pending.
